          "redirectURL": "",
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":528,\"filmId\":385,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-07-26T18:00\",\"doorsTime\":\"5:30pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6:00pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":3,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":385,\"title\":\"THE HONEYMOON KILLERS\",\"description\":\"A lonely nurse in upstate New York becomes involved with a charismatic con man, and together they embark on a crime spree targeting lonely, overweight women through personal ads. As their partnership intensifies, their relationship becomes as unstable and destructive as the murders they commit.\\n\\nLeonard Kastle’s film takes a stark, almost documentary approach to true-crime material, stripping away glamour in favour of procedural detail and emotional bleakness. Its restrained style and focus on character dysfunction give the story a cold, matter-of-fact brutality that contrasts with more sensational crime dramas.\",\"runtime\":108,\"year\":1970,\"country\":\"USA\",\"director\":\"Leonard Kastle\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://player.bfi.org.uk/sites/default/files/hero-images/Honeymoon_Killers_6-1920.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
