            "text": "{\"id\":530,\"filmId\":280,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-07-27T18:30\",\"doorsTime\":\"6:00pm\",\"filmTime\":\"6:30pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":0,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":280,\"title\":\"PUNK AT 50 PRESENTS: RODRIGO D: NO FUTURO\",\"description\":\"SCREENING AS PART OF **PUNK! AT 50**\\n\\nRodrigo and his friends are bored teenagers living in the slums of Medellín, Colombia. Rodrigo dreams of starting a punk band, but with no opportunities and constant exposure to crime, violence, and aimlessness, he and his mates drift through their days stealing bikes or cars, listening to music, and trying to find meaning in a world that feels stacked against them.\\n\\nThis raw, unflinching drama paints a vivid portrait of youth pushed to the margins. With naturalistic performances from young non‑professional actors and a soundtrack rooted in punk energy, the film captures both the bleakness and the restless spirit of life in late‑1980s Medellín, where dreams flicker and futures feel impossible to grasp.\",\"runtime\":93,\"year\":1990,\"country\":\"Colombia\",\"director\":\"Víctor Gaviria\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://images.mubicdn.net/images/film/21599/cache-14203-1745489725/image-w1280.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
