          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":537,\"filmId\":397,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-07-30T20:45\",\"doorsTime\":\"8:20pm\",\"filmTime\":\"8:45pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":3,\"price\":1100,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":397,\"title\":\"THAT OBSCURE OBJECT OF DESIRE\",\"description\":\"A wealthy middle-aged man becomes infatuated with a young woman he meets during a train journey, initiating a turbulent and frustrating pursuit of her affection. Despite repeated encounters, she continually eludes his attempts at intimacy, appearing in shifting contexts that complicate his understanding of who she is and what she wants.\\n\\nLuis Buñuel structures the narrative around repetition and contradiction, with the same events retold from different perspectives, emphasizing instability in perception and desire. The film’s fragmented storytelling and surreal interruptions create a constant tension between romantic obsession and psychological uncertainty.\",\"runtime\":103,\"year\":1977,\"country\":\"France, Spain\",\"director\":\"Luis Buñuel\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/editorial_content_posts/hero/7233-/yZhW0zjGbVNJeI2YqzUReSbgXO3LZ3_original.jpg\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"15\"}}",
