          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"id\":544,\"filmId\":430,\"screeningDate\":\"2026-08-09T17:00\",\"doorsTime\":\"4:15pm\",\"filmTime\":\"5:00pm\",\"capacity\":37,\"ticketsSold\":3,\"price\":1350,\"format\":\"Digital\",\"excludeFromGiftVouchers\":false,\"isPrivate\":false,\"memberOnly\":false,\"film\":{\"id\":430,\"title\":\"TFFF: SITTING IDLE + Q&A\",\"description\":\"A meandering, meditative visual poem that follows the life of a nameless character over the course of a year - as he traverses across the country, meeting and living with friends along the way. Sitting Idle presents an unconventional plot-free narrative that acts as a visual longitudinal study and diary - exploring feelings of loneliness, alienation, and jadedness amid the death throes of a decaying urban landscape and changing social climate. A major global event looms. \\n\\nThis UK Premiere will be followed by a Q&A with the director Luke Olutunmogun.\",\"runtime\":86,\"year\":null,\"country\":\"UK\",\"director\":\"Luke Olutunmogun\",\"imageUrl\":\"https://yxvwcvyczjjes5ua.public.blob.vercel-storage.com/Screenshot%202026-06-29%20at%2011.56.00.png\",\"imageCropX\":50,\"imageCropY\":50,\"ageCertificate\":\"18\"}}",
